  "cover": {
    "_note": "Interpreted land cover of about 1800, not survey data. Each sample says what kind of ground lies around a point; ground is blended between samples by distance, then a few Natural Earth region outlines override it. Samples follow the broad vegetation belts (tundra, taiga, mixed and broadleaf forest, forest-steppe, steppe, semi-desert, Mediterranean, desert) with western Europe drawn more open than the east, as it was after centuries of clearing. 'champaign' is long-cleared, closely farmed lowland (the Paris basin, Flanders, the Po plain, the English Midlands, Saxony): the open country where the period's great battles were fought.",
